{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>And He rained down</b> — The sense: and He had already rained down upon them, as in: 'And YHWH Elohim formed' [Genesis 2:8] — and He had already formed. 'And YHWH said to Moses' — and He had already said. 'And they journeyed from Rephidim' [Exodus 17:1] — and they had already journeyed. 'And he said: Whose daughter are you?' [Genesis 24:23] — and he had already said. 'And he said to Moses: I am your father-in-law' [Exodus 18:6] — and afterward 'And he came' [Exodus 18:7]. And many are like this. And the reason [is]: Why did they crave meat? To test HaShem. And what need did they have for meat, when they had the manna, which was sweet and pleasant and clean, and they gathered it without toil, for free?! And 'He struck the rock for them' [Numbers 20:11] — and they had water to drink — [therefore] he said: <b>And He rained down</b>, for it came down from the sky, and <b>grain of the heavens</b>, for it is born in the air."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 78, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:35:04.589201095Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}